    { hype: 'Hyperscalers have unlimited capacity to fund AI.', reality: 'Alphabet tapping Canadian bond markets and raising $17B in debt shows even the largest tech companies are stretching for leverage. The GPU capacity race has real financing constraints.' },
  ],
  infraHealthCheck: 'CVE-2026-43284 "Dirty Frag" is being actively exploited to escape containers in multi-tenant environments. Any Linux host with esp4 or rxrpc networking components enabled is at risk. This is a "Zero-Race" exploit — more reliable than previous privilege escalation methods. Patch before your next maintenance window.',
  legacySpotlight: 'The Equiniti acquisition by Bullish ($4.2B) suggests crypto exchanges are pivoting toward traditional financial outsourcing to stabilize revenue against crypto volatility. Legacy financial infrastructure providers are becoming acquisition targets for digital-native firms seeking stable, regulated revenue streams.',
}

const builderUtility = {
  toolOfTheWeek: {
    name: 'Linux Kernel LivePatch (for Dirty Frag)',
    description: 'With CVE-2026-43284 being actively exploited in multi-tenant container environments, kernel livepatch tools (Canonical Livepatch, kpatch, KernelCare) are this week\'s essential utility. They allow patching the esp4/rxrpc vulnerability without rebooting production hosts — critical for teams running 24/7 workloads who cannot afford a maintenance window.',
    source: 'Canonical',
    sourceUrl: 'https://ubuntu.com/security/livepatch',
  },
  codeSnippet: {
    title: 'Check & Mitigate Dirty Frag Exposure',
    language: 'bash',
    code: '# Check if vulnerable kernel modules are loaded\nlsmod | grep -E "esp4|rxrpc"\n\n# If loaded, disable until patched\nsudo modprobe -r esp4 rxrpc 2>/dev/null\n\n# Block reloading via modprobe blacklist\necho "blacklist esp4" | sudo tee /etc/modprobe.d/dirty-frag.conf\necho "blacklist rxrpc" | sudo tee -a /etc/modprobe.d/dirty-frag.conf\n\n# Verify kernel version (patch when available)\nuname -r\n\n# Apply livepatch if available (Ubuntu)\nsudo canonical-livepatch status',
  },
  securityAlert: 'CVE-2026-43284 "Dirty Frag" — Linux Kernel local privilege escalation via networking components esp4 and rxrpc. Actively exploited for container escapes in multi-tenant environments. Patch immediately on all Linux-based hosts (Ubuntu, RHEL, openSUSE).',
}

